#############################################################
# Example notecard for the LuaSitter [LS]chains plugin.
#############################################################
//
// Put this notecard, named "[LS]chains_settings", and the [LS]chains script
// in the prim with the [LS]sit scripts. Name the prims the chains go to
// (for example "ring1", "ring2"...). Full guide: docs/luasitter/chains.md
//
// Lines starting with # or // are comments, and so is anything after //.
//
// STYLE lockguard|<LockGuard parameters>
//     Chains for LockGuard V2 cuffs. Parameters: size x y, life seconds,
//     gravity g, color r g b, texture uuid (left out: the cuff's own look).
// STYLE lockmeister|<particle settings>
//     Chains for LockMeister cuffs, drawn from the ring prim:
//     size x y, life seconds, gravity g, color r g b, texture uuid.
// The first STYLE line also chooses the protocol of the CHAIN lines
// (LockGuard when there is no STYLE line).
//
// CHAIN pose|sitter|cuff,ring,cuff,ring...
//     pose: the menu name of a POSE or SYNC, or * for any pose.
//     sitter: 0, 1... or * for any sitter.
//     Then cuff and ring prim pairs. An empty list (or none) means no chains.
//     Add |lockmeister or |lockguard at the end to use the other protocol.
//     The most precise line wins: pose|sitter, pose|*, *|sitter, *|*.
//
// TOGGLE on|off            extra link numbers that switch the chains on / off
// TOGGLE on|off|toggle     (90240 on, 90241 off, 90242 toggle always work), so
//                          menu buttons of older products keep working.
// PROPS 1                  LockGuard rings may be in props ([LS]LockGuard-object).
//
// Menu buttons (in LSpos / AVpos):
//     BUTTON Chains|90242
//
#############################################################

STYLE lockguard|size 0.08 0.08 life 0.6 gravity 0.6 texture d7277e78-06f4-58ae-9f7c-7499e50de18a

// Wrists to the wall rings in "Kneel", for any sitter
CHAIN Kneel|*|leftwrist,ring1,rightwrist,ring2

// No chains in "Rest"
CHAIN Rest|*|none

// Every other pose of sitter 0: the ankles
CHAIN *|0|leftankle,ring3,rightankle,ring4

// Old products used link messages 98 (on) and 99 (off)
TOGGLE 98|99
